*.bundle
*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.local
configurations/
mockup/
tools/flash2html/output/
*.png

# ...except the website's own, which are not dump-derived and which nothing regenerates. The blanket
# rule above caught them by accident, and the result only appears in a deployment: a clone has no
# sprite sheet, so the site builds with no logo, no navigation icons and no currencies.
#
# It builds GREEN, which is what makes this worth a comment. Vite leaves an unresolvable
# `new URL('../assets/sprite.png', import.meta.url)` as a literal string instead of failing, so the
# browser asks for a path that does not exist and the SPA fallback answers index.html with a 200 —
# an image request served HTML, reported nowhere.
!packages/vortex-web/src/assets/*.png
!packages/vortex-web/public/**/*.png

# Window layouts/skins extracted from a Habbo dump by tools/build-window-assets.mjs, and
# the sound effects extracted by tools/import-crypted-sounds.mjs. Derived dump content,
# like sources/, configurations/ and *.png above: generated per checkout, never committed.
packages/vortex-client/src/assets/window-layouts/
packages/vortex-client/src/assets/window-skins/
packages/vortex-client/src/assets/sounds/
NUL
tmp/
# Dev-only esbuild pre-bundle of vortex-engine, rebuilt on every `pnpm dev`
# by packages/vortex-client/tools/vite-plugin-engine-bundle.mjs.
packages/vortex-client/.vortex-dev/

# `:stresstest` frame-budget runs, written by tools/vite-plugin-perf-log.mjs.
# Anchored to the repo root: a bare `perf/` also swallows source directories named perf,
# which is what hid packages/vortex-engine/src/habbo/perf from git.
/perf/

# Scratch self-check scripts: never committed.
*.check.ts

# Local-only tooling. The measurement probes, the one-off checks and the Director
# extraction scripts are personal working tools, not part of what is shared. The
# pre-commit hook and the Claude PostToolUse hook both guard on their presence, so
# a clone without them still commits normally.
/scripts/

# The port's own progress tracking, and the tool that regenerates it. Working notes,
# not documentation for anyone else.
/docs/status.yaml

# Python bytecode from scripts/origins/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# vortex-client-assets.zip is the ONE piece of derived dump content that IS committed, and it is
# deliberately absent from the list above. Everything else here is gitignored because it is
# regenerated per checkout from a dump — but a clone has no dump, so that rule left it unable to
# draw anything at all. The archive is what makes `git clone && node install.mjs` sufficient on
# its own. Re-pack and commit it whenever the dump changes: `node install.mjs --pack`.
